  "content": "The Caro-Kann, like the Sicilian Defense and French Defense, is classified as a \"semi-open game\", but it is thought to be more passive and drawish than either of those openings.\nThe opening is named after the German players Horatio Caro and Marcus Kann who analyzed the opening in 1886.\nAccording to Chessbase, black chances are about 43%",
